windows-scripts
---------------

This sets up the Windows editor and search tools used on development
machines. Run PowerShell as Administrator, then:

    iex (iwr https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ninjaasmoke/windows-scripts/refs/heads/main/setup.ps1 -UseBasicParsing).Content

The script installs Everything, Neovim, fd, ripgrep, and
JetBrainsMono Nerd Font. It installs the official LazyVim starter in
%LOCALAPPDATA%\nvim. If that directory exists, the script first copies it to
a timestamped %LOCALAPPDATA%\nvim.backup-* directory.

Using Neovim
------------

Open a project from its working directory:

    nvim .

Neovim is installed for all users and its installer adds
%ProgramFiles%\Neovim\bin to the system PATH. Open a new terminal after setup
if the current terminal cannot find nvim.

LazyVim provides a file tree and filename search. The additional Git views
use these keys:

    <leader>gg    open Neogit status, staging, and commit UI
    <leader>gd    open Diffview

In LazyVim, <leader> is the Space key.


GVFS repositories
-----------------

The setup does not modify or reinstall VFS for Git/GVFS and does not run
automatic Git operations. LazyVim, Neogit, and Diffview only inspect a
repository when invoked.
